 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nParagraphFormat.left_indent returns incorrect values\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `left_indent` property of `ParagraphFormat` is returning unexpected values. When a paragraph has no formatting properties, it should return `None`, but it's returning `0` instead. Additionally, when there are formatting properties present, the returned value appears to be off by 1.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom docx import Document\nfrom docx.shared import Inches\n\n# Create a new document\ndoc = Document()\n\n# Add a paragraph with no formatting\np1 = doc.add_paragraph(\"No formatting\")\nprint(f\"Expected: None, Got: {p1.paragraph_format.left_indent}\")\n\n# Add a paragraph with left indent\np2 = doc.add_paragraph(\"With indent\")\np2.paragraph_format.left_indent = Inches(0.5)\nprint(f\"Expected: {Inches(0.5)}, Got: {p2.paragraph_format.left_indent}\")\n```\n\nThe output shows that paragraphs without formatting return `0` instead of `None`, and paragraphs with formatting return values that are 1 unit higher than expected.\n</issue>\n",
